{"agent":"bugfixL","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_cell` still folds only `\\n`, so a carriage return passes straight through: `run_cli(repo, \"task\", \"add\", \"T1\", \"--phase\", \"P1\", \"--title\", \"a\\rb\")` stores the CR unchanged, and the row emitted by `table()` becomes `| [ ] | **T1** a\\rb | todo | — | — | ... |` with a raw U+000D inside the title cell. CommonMark defines a lone carriage return (`U+000D` not followed by `U+000A`) as a line ending, so a GFM/cmark-gfm parser normalizes it to `\\n` and splits the row into two lines — precisely the corruption class this bug is about (the new regression test only exercises `\\n`, so it does not catch this). The fix's own docstring claims \"newlines folded\", but `\\r` and `\\r\\n` (which becomes `\\r ` — the CR is not removed, only the LF is) are both left intact. The title survives storage unmodified (YAML/JSON emit `\\r` as an escaped scalar and restore it on load), so this input is reachable. Folding `\\r\\n?` (or splitting/joining `splitlines()`) is needed for the fix to actually cover the stated bug.","digest":"ac9137c694dbb89b","location":"ddflow/views/markdown.py — `_cell` (`folded = _redact(text, cfg).replace(\"\\n\", \" \")`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/views/markdown.py — `_cell` (`folded = _redact(text, cfg).replace(\"\\n\", \" \")`)"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3978,"diff_sha":"d34fd257b5fffb6b451728fc12c791d990e753f2f2fde8bbe37e77ffce646e3d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in /home/delian/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B2eaa1e5e8e","elapsed_s":156.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"3c034878cd1f659c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B2eaa1e5e8e.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261005T172022-efc654c0.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewe